            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous regression of post-percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty aneurysm.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>233-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of a 67-year-old male with spontaneous regression of post-percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty (PTCA) aneurysm. This case substantiates the benign prognosis of post-PTCA aneurysms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
